--
Regression test for character access on a literally-constructed std::string.

libstdc++ provides std::__cxx11::basic_string<char> as an explicit
instantiation declaration (extern template).  CBMC realises that class via
the incomplete-to-complete swap in typecheck_compound_type rather than via
instantiate_template, so its inline character-copy helpers
_S_copy_chars/_S_copy used to keep an un-converted body that clean_up()
discarded, making the copy a no-op (size() was correct but the characters
were non-deterministic).

queue_deferred_methods_of_instance() now instantiates those inline member
bodies at the instance-completion site, per N5008 [temp.inst]/4 and Note 4.
This test was previously KNOWNBUG; it became CORE once the fix landed.
